// toolbox/scrap.cla: curated Scrap Manager (desk scrap) declarations
// (Inside Macintosh I, "The Scrap Manager"). All pascal-convention
// (bit 11 set). TEFromScrap/TEToScrap are deliberately ABSENT: they are
// glue routines with no trap word (see the cookbook's copy/paste
// walkthrough), not Scrap Manager traps -- also confirmed by
// runtime/clarus/uitext.cla's own doc comment, which found no
// TE-prefixed entries in Retro68 multiversal/defs/ScrapMgr.yaml either.
//
// Provenance: ZeroScrap proven verbatim against runtime/clarus/ui.cla's
// UiZeroScrap (0xA9FC). PutScrap (0xA9FE) and GetScrap (0xA9FD) were
// originally verified against multiversal defs/ScrapMgr.yaml per
// runtime/clarus/uitext.cla:144-145's comment. InfoScrap (0xA9F9),
// LoadScrap (0xA9FB), UnloadScrap (0xA9FA), and the ScrapStuff
// peek-offset table below were likewise originally checked only against
// defs/ScrapMgr.yaml's own `function:`/`struct: ScrapStuff` entries.
//
// Apple-interfaces re-verification (toolbox-cookbook phase, 2026-08-07):
// multiversal/defs/*.yaml is a third-party reconstruction and UNTRUSTED
// WHEN CITED ALONE -- a citation it is the SOLE source for has never been
// checked against Apple at all. (The anecdote that used to justify this
// rule here -- that multiversal put Gestalt's `responsep` in the wrong
// register -- was itself wrong, and pack3-standardfile Task 5a retired
// it: multiversal's `Out<A0>` was RIGHT, and our A1 reading came from
// taking `Gestalt.h`'s `#pragma parameter` line as the trap's contract
// when it describes the INLINE GLUE. The sharper rule that survives:
// decode the inline words -- a `TWOWORDINLINE` routine's second word is
// glue you must reproduce or route around. See toolbox/osutils.cla.)
// Every trap word and the ScrapStuff layout
// below are now confirmed directly against Apple's own Universal
// Interfaces 3.4 (Retro68/InterfacesAndLibraries/Interfaces): AIncludes/
// Scrap.a confirms ZeroScrap $A9FC / GetScrap $A9FD / PutScrap $A9FE /
// InfoScrap $A9F9 / LoadScrap $A9FB / UnloadScrap $A9FA, and CIncludes/
// Scrap.h:125-131's `struct ScrapStuff` (scrapSize: SInt32, scrapHandle:
// Handle, scrapCount: SInt16, scrapState: SInt16, scrapName: StringPtr,
// declared in that order) lays out to the same sequential offsets/sizes
// 0/4/8/$A/$C, size $10, listed below -- multiversal citations above are
// secondary corroboration only, superseded by this direct check.
//
// InfoScrap returns a pointer to the ScrapStuff record; read it with
// peek at these offsets (no extern-record conversion exists for a
// returned ptr):
//   +0  scrapSize    long   (peekl)
//   +4  scrapHandle  Handle (peekl)
//   +8  scrapCount   word   (peekw)
//   +10 scrapState   word   (peekw)
//   +12 scrapName    ptr    (peekl)

external func ZeroScrap(): int = trap 0xA9FC
external func PutScrap(length: int, theType: int, source: ptr): int = trap 0xA9FE
external func GetScrap(hDest: ptr, theType: int, offset: ptr): int = trap 0xA9FD
external func InfoScrap(): ptr = trap 0xA9F9
external func LoadScrap(): int = trap 0xA9FB
external func UnloadScrap(): int = trap 0xA9FA
